{lo re palku} = "the two pants" which means that you are referring to
two separate pants, not one pants which are "the second".  If I heard
someone say {ca lo cabdei mi dasni le vo palku} I would think that they were
saying "today I wore 4 different pairs of pants" which is clearly not what
you're trying to say.

On Sat, Jan 29, 2011 at 10:33 PM, Oren <get.oren@gmail.com> wrote:

